you've probably seen these fun colorful  tasty fish cakes in your ramen bowls or  udon and soba noodle dishes  they're called fish cakes and these  little side pieces have a long and  powerful history in japan  [Music]  fish cakes have existed in japanese  cuisine since the 8th century  over the years various kinds of fish  cakes have been developed but there is  one kind of fish cake that has stood the  test of time  it's called hen pen  often made from a fish meat called  pollock these fluffy white fish cakes  are considered the ogs of fish cakes and  some of the best hand pens are made here  by this guy  a legendary fish cake shop that's been  selling and making hen pen since 1688  foreign  [Music]  [Music]  may not be as colorful as its fish cake  counterparts but people love it  these fish cakes are in such demand  during peak season that toshio produces  about four thousand handpins in a day  [Music]  hamper  surprisingly after four decades toshio  has not grown tired of making handpins  because for him it's more than just a  job  musical  [Music]
 

